<title>GERMANY: German inland gas oil falls with IPE futures.</title>
<headline>German inland gas oil falls with IPE futures.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.7060)   DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     32.70/33.10     19.17/19.41   32.80/33.20</p>
<p> BREMEN		32.70/33.10     19.17/19.41   32.80/33.20</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    32.80/33.50     19.24/19.65   32.90/33.60</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   33.30/33.80     19.53/19.82   33.50/34.00</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   33.20/33.60     18.88/19.35   33.30/33.80</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  34.20/34.80     20.06/20.41   35.00/35.40</p>
<p>German inland gas oil fell again with weaker gas oil futures, traders said on Tuesday. Mild weather and the absence of any signs of a sustained cold snap has led to relaxed buyers, traders said. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8980</p>
</text>
